{
  "source": "Prompts/embrace-the-future-opener-v7.mp4",
  "duration": 187.2,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.2,
      "text": "Up to this point, you've learned exactly how to use AI in your daily life."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.74,
      "end": 8.88,
      "text": "You understand the underlying engine running it, which means that when the model behaves"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.88,
      "end": 12.84,
      "text": "strangely, that strange behavior actually makes perfect sense to you."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.28,
      "end": 16.5,
      "text": "Your initial goal for this course was to be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.02,
      "end": 18.04,
      "text": "Consider that done."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.78,
      "end": 23.32,
      "text": "But understanding how a tool works mechanically doesn't automatically tell us how it will"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.32,
      "end": 24.92,
      "text": "impact society in the long run."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.32,
      "end": 28.68,
      "text": "There's the optimist, who thinks AI is completely fantastic."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.68,
      "end": 32.08,
      "text": "There's the warrior, who was convinced it will hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.88,
      "end": 35.2,
      "text": "Here's the honest part, nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.06,
      "end": 39.58,
      "text": "Not them, not us, not the people building AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.34,
      "end": 46.3,
      "text": "Centuries ago, map makers had to chart vast expanses of ocean they simply did not understand yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.92,
      "end": 51.46,
      "text": "Whenever they reached the edges of their knowledge, they would fill the blank waters with imaginary"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.46,
      "end": 53.7,
      "text": "sea monsters and strange serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.26,
      "end": 58.2,
      "text": "The future of AI is like the unknown parts of the ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.0,
      "end": 65.14,
      "text": "Warriors fill the unknown parts with AI monsters that destroy jobs, hack systems, and take over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.84,
      "end": 71.22,
      "text": "AI optimists look at the same unknown parts and see easy, clear sailing through open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.94,
      "end": 76.4,
      "text": "Both the utopian and dystopian extremes are just modern versions of those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.06,
      "end": 82.1,
      "text": "When people lack facts about a blank space, they draw their own fears and hopes to fill it."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.6,
      "end": 86.84,
      "text": "History shows us that early sailors never actually encountered literal sea monsters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.5,
      "end": 89.94,
      "text": "but they also rarely got easy, clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.74,
      "end": 93.42,
      "text": "Instead, they usually found something entirely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.36,
      "end": 95.76,
      "text": "Consider Ferdinand Magellan."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.36,
      "end": 99.6,
      "text": "He never actually set off to sail around the world,"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.04,
      "end": 102.68,
      "text": "but his crew ended up achieving exactly that."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.3,
      "end": 109.34,
      "text": "And Magellan himself met a tragic end, dying before the historic voyage was even completed."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.0,
      "end": 111.06,
      "text": "Did he expect either?"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.64,
      "end": 111.9,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.4,
      "end": 116.78,
      "text": "So as we move forward, we are going to take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.76,
      "end": 120.96,
      "text": "We will look at the monsters, and we will look at the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.66,
      "end": 124.68,
      "text": "Right now, there is only one absolute certainty."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.18,
      "end": 126.82,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.48,
      "end": 131.84,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it will keep getting better forever, just that it isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.42,
      "end": 137.22,
      "text": "Because this technology is a permanent fixture with a trajectory we can't fully predict,"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.64,
      "end": 141.18,
      "text": "our best path forward is to prepare for unexpected realities,"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.76,
      "end": 143.76,
      "text": "rather than clinging to extreme predictions."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.82,
      "end": 147.42,
      "text": "This road map shows what will explore in this section."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.88,
      "end": 148.86,
      "text": "Embrace the future."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.84,
      "end": 150.78,
      "text": "1. The argument."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.62,
      "end": 152.28,
      "text": "The loudest voices."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.0,
      "end": 153.5,
      "text": "Why they disagree."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.3,
      "end": 156.3,
      "text": "And why the speed makes the argument louder."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.42,
      "end": 159.52,
      "text": "2. Monsters and open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.16,
      "end": 164.92,
      "text": "The honest case for worry alongside the real world upside that has already happened."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.92,
      "end": 167.64,
      "text": "3. Wear it lands on you."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.36,
      "end": 169.3,
      "text": "How AI acts."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.76,
      "end": 170.7,
      "text": "How work may change."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.5,
      "end": 172.56,
      "text": "The bill for all that math."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.18,
      "end": 174.92,
      "text": "And what history teaches about predictions."
    },
    {
      "start": 176.16,
      "end": 177.84,
      "text": "Take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 178.82,
      "end": 180.3,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.9,
      "end": 182.68,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    }
  ],
